=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# users screen-root-login --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: User Management. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13.$
# hardn's host, but hardn runs from a root login (su -, root's$
# key): no SUDO_USER, so the session user isn't known. Removing$
# george's grant is refused, as george is the last admin; every$
# key removal is typed.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           hardn$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]:$
$
$

